  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively denote the centroid, circumcentre and orthocentre of a triangle. Then, the distance of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> measured parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>",
